<onlyinclude>'''Group cognition''' concerns the cognitive processes that occur through interaction within a group. Participants may construct shared meanings, solve problems or maintain common representations through conversation and joint activity.

== Explanation ==
A team drawing a diagram together may develop a solution that none of its members initially had. Each contribution changes what others can see and do. Group cognition studies this process; it does not require a literal shared consciousness.

